James inquired about terminology for benefit-cost ratios (BCRs) that focus on benefits and costs incurred in a specific year, contrasting with the standard multi-year calculation (NPV). I explained that no widely accepted special term exists but suggested common phrases such as "annual benefit–cost ratio," "year-t benefit–cost ratio," and "undiscounted annual BCR" for clarity. For formal notation, I provided equations differentiating the year-t BCR from the standard NPV-based BCR. I recommended using “static (year-t) BCR” and “dynamic (NPV) BCR” in his work to ensure clarity and avoid misinterpretation.
